# Azure OpenAI connection settings used by both notebooks
# (code_03_XX Router notebook and code_06_XX Customer Service notebook).
#
# Copy this file to ".env" in the project root and fill in the three
# values below. ".env" is git-ignored, so your real key never gets
# committed — only this template (.env.example) should be checked in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# How to get these values
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. You need an Azure subscription with access to Azure OpenAI
#    (Azure AI Foundry). If you don't have a resource yet:
#      Azure Portal -> "Create a resource" -> search "Azure OpenAI"
#      -> create the resource (pick a region that has the models you
#      need, e.g. East US, since not all regions carry every model).
#
# 2. Deploy the models this course uses, in Azure AI Foundry
#    (https://ai.azure.com) or Azure OpenAI Studio, under
#    your resource -> "Deployments" -> "Create new deployment":
#      - a chat model (e.g. gpt-4o / gpt-4o-mini, or whatever current
#        chat model your subscription has access to)
#      - an embedding model (e.g. text-embedding-ada-002 or
#        text-embedding-3-small)
#    You choose a "deployment name" for each when creating it — these
#    are NOT set in this .env file. They're passed as the
#    `deployment_name` argument directly in the notebook code
#    (currently "agentai-gpt35"/"agentai-gpt4" and "agentai-embedding").
#    Update those in-notebook values to match whatever deployment
#    names you actually create.
#
# 3. Get the key and endpoint for AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY and
#    AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT from:
#      Azure Portal -> your Azure OpenAI resource -> left menu
#      "Resource Management" -> "Keys and Endpoint"
#    Either KEY 1 or KEY 2 works. The endpoint looks like:
#      https://<your-resource-name>.openai.azure.com/
#
# 4. AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION is the Azure OpenAI REST API version
#    string (not the model version), e.g. "2024-05-01-preview".
#    Check the current supported list here:
#      https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/reference
#    Use a version that supports the features you need (chat
#    completions + embeddings are supported by all recent versions).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# From: Azure Portal -> your resource -> Keys and Endpoint -> KEY 1
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# From: Azure Portal -> your resource -> Keys and Endpoint -> Endpoint
# Format: https://<your-resource-name>.openai.azure.com/
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=

# Azure OpenAI REST API version, e.g. 2024-05-01-preview
AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=
